     note: "Deliberately not marked `quotation`: the hedge 'A case can be made that' sits just outside the span, and the claim is the reported proposal, not the authors' assertion."}
    <+ [Aphantasics use spatial strategies]: Aphantasics often use spatial and sensorimotor
      strategies to solve visual working memory tasks, and mental rotation is a task perfectly
      suited for spatial imagery. #reported
        {fidelity: "compression", pinpoint: "§4.2",
         source: "\"aphantasics often use spatial (and sensorimotor) strategies to solve visual working memory tasks\""}
(2) [Spatial imagery could carry the custom]: A custom to imagine a range of spatial images in
    response to a general term would be enough for Humean abstraction. #reported
    {fidelity: "interpretation", warrant: "enthymeme", pinpoint: "§4.2",
     source: "\"If Humean abstraction requires forming a custom to imagine a range of individual ideas that fall under a general term in response to a single individual idea associated with the term, couldn't severe aphantasics just perform abstraction by forming a custom to imagine a range of spatial images?\"",
     note: "The step the rhetorical question invites, imputed to the response rather than to the authors, who go on to deny it."}
